Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: expose Houji stock display and thermal state

Stock xm_batt_update_work polls XM116 (THERMAL_TEMP). Its panel notifier
forwards blank state via XM117. Expose only the verified scalar ABI to the
charging owner. Preserve the existing capacity source and FCC protections.
Do not couple USB liquid-port detection to the display on this port: Type-C
and moisture handling have a separate owner.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -2315,6 +2315,8 @@
 HOUJI_XM_RO(charger_user_value_map, 13, false);
 HOUJI_XM_RO(smart_chg, 131, false);
 HOUJI_XM_RO(fg1_rsoc, 195, false);
+HOUJI_XM_RO(thermal_temp, 116, false);
+HOUJI_XM_BOOL(fb_blank_state, 117);
 HOUJI_XM_RO(connector_temp, 2, false);
 static struct houji_xm_attribute houji_attr_thermal_board_temp = {
 	.attr = __ATTR(thermal_board_temp, 0600, houji_xm_show, houji_board_temp_store),
@@ -2621,4 +2623,6 @@
 	&houji_attr_fg1_rsoc.attr.attr,
+	&houji_attr_thermal_temp.attr.attr,
+	&houji_attr_fb_blank_state.attr.attr,
 	&houji_attr_connector_temp.attr.attr,
 	&houji_attr_thermal_board_temp.attr.attr,
 	&houji_attr_fastchg_mode.attr.attr,
